WEBVTT

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:11.740
Go forth and tussle it out!

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.340
Alright! That was a great half!

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.350
This match is ours!

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.580
We did quite well.

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:09.950
A comfortable 2-0 lead going into the 2nd half.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:15.890
I was hoping for a bit more from your side,

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:18.730
Tatsumi Takeshi.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.750
What the hell were you doing, Sugie?

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:26.470
Kuro!

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:27.730
Hey, Kuroda!

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:28.750
Hey, what's up?

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:31.500
Do you even know what you're supposed to do?

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:37.300
You're supposed to choke up the opponent's attacks by marking Kubota!

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.200
Instead, he keeps getting the loose balls!

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.390
That's why their attacks are never-ending!

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.980
Getting yourself embarrassed by some kid!

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:48.270
Aren't you ashamed?!

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:52.720
They're noisy. Baki, go stop them.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.270
What? Me?!

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.970
Leave them be.

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:59.530
It's not like they'll start throwing punches.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.010
This plan depends...

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:08.780
... on you finding a way to deal with Kubota while I keep Hauer in check.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:13.210
But I lost against him.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:20.050
And instead of putting pressure on Kubota, you're letting him do as he pleases!

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:23.300
We're the centre-backs, Sugie!

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.560
This is unacceptable!

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.810
If the heart of the defense is failing, the team won't win!

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:39.520
That's why, you guys! Go ahead and hit us!

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:40.330
Come on!

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.070
Huh? Why?

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.120
Come on!

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.970
This is kinda creepy.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.110
That's enough, Kuroda.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:49.210
It's not like it's all your fault.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:54.960
I miscalculated the timing of the cross. I was hesitant in rushing out too.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:58.230
It's the fault of the entire defense.

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:09.520
Crap!

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.240
That's right,

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:19.150
the first goal was due to my mistake.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.220
Kubota's goal...

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:36.170
I allowed Hatake's pass through too easily.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:43.220
As I expected, the atmosphere here is terrible!

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:49.060
You should hurry up, Tatsumi! Where are you anyway?!

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:54.770
That was a great 1st half, lads. I really enjoyed myself.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:05:01.000
Listen to me, manager! This guy plays way too selfishly!

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.380
What are you saying? Don't blame others for your lousy performance!

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:08.830
I'm talking about your pointless dribbling. Right, Hauer?!

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:11.700
You know,

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.460
I'd prefer passes that come to my foot.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.580
When I head the ball, my hair gets messed up.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.090
What? You dare to complain?!

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.300
You are bad with your feet!

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:25.320
Complain some more and I'll shave you bald!

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:25.610
Someone bring a shaver!

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:27.090
Don't touch me!

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.850
If you don't want that, create some openings for me!

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:34.390
As usual, the forwards are kicking up a fuss during the half time break.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.540
They're just excited.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:42.360
They all want to score more goals.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:45.240
Not scoring against them is impossible.

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:47.550
Their defense is full of holes!

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:50.240
The person marking me is not much of note either.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:56.250
Yeah. Thanks to the poor matchup, Hauer got more of the balls than usual.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:00.400
Kubo didn't lose to Sugie too. Right, Kubo?

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:06.760
Uh... um... probably.

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:09.790
Their offense is no good either.

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:12.200
They only managed to get one shot on goal.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:15.050
Gino's passes are really off.

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:19.270
Which is why they're unable to execute their trademark speedy attacks.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:23.580
If Gino's still the playmaker in the 2nd half,

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:26.280
our defense has nothing to fear about.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:31.280
To sum it up, it boils down to this,

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:34.630
I don't feel like we'll lose to ETU today.

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:36.790
We'll dominate the game in the 2nd half as well...

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:39.040
and get a big scoreline!

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:44.300
Looks like I've got nothing to worry about.

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:49.590
You guys are full of passion and brimming with confidence.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:55.390
Don't worry. There's no way you guys can lose.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:03.190
This is what I said, the face of winners.

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:05.690
Whoa.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:11.200
What's wrong?

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:13.950
Don't you feel that the atmosphere's very dull?

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:18.780
Tatsumi, where have you been? The half time break's almost over.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:20.460
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:23.960
Hey, can you guys bring out some drive?

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:28.510
How are you supposed to do interesting things with such dull faces?

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:32.470
Our big comeback is about to begin.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:37.920
What big comeback? We're already two goals behind!

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:39.230
Two!

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:46.860
Manager, your plan was for us to spend the 1st half defending with all we've got.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:50.860
And even if we do let them score, we should keep it at one.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:55.090
However, now that the momentum's with them having scored twice,

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:57.490
can we really go against them in the 2nd half?

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:01.250
What?

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:03.370
Kuro...

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:07.250
Are you enjoying this match?

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:08.880
What about you, Sugie?

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:11.380
Having fun?

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:14.890
Oh my, what's the matter?

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:19.490
Something's wrong.

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:23.030
Even the coach here looks dull.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:24.400
This is no good.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:30.780
What's up with that? Am I the only one who thinks that this match will turn out to be interesting?

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:31.900
Huh?

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:34.590
I told you guys.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:39.660
The most important thing is whether you guys can enjoy the match.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:51.220
So I went around and asked three ball boys and two cameramen this,

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:52.210
What?

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:58.710
"What would you think if ETU were to turn the game around in the 2nd half and win?"

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:02.190
Wait, that's what you were doing just now?!

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:06.190
Yup. Though they were kinda nervous and didn't want to answer.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:12.070
Amongst them, a young man courageously said,

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:16.950
"If that happened, I think it would be a really interesting game."

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:22.700
In the end, everyone there agreed with his view.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:24.710
Don't you get it?

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:29.430
They might have said that just because I'm ETU's manager,

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:32.210
but I'm pretty sure most people feel that way.

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:35.090
Even I feel the same too.

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:39.720
It's true that we might get humiliated even more...

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.720
But you know,

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:48.620
if we get to overturn this two-goal handicap; two, not just one...

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.210
It'll be way more fun!

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:55.490
H-Hey...

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:58.090
Well, manager...

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:01.880
You can keep saying it like it doesn't concern you,

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.740
but we're the ones who'll actually have to do it.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:06.390
I know, Kuro.

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:08.750
I'm telling you this because I believe in you.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:09.710
Huh?

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:12.980
The 1st half was completely dominated by Osaka.

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:15.390
From a spectator's point of view,

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:17.760
that's an expected outcome.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:19.230
However,

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:22.760
what you can see with your eyes isn't everything.

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:27.520
Don't worry. You guys have done your jobs well.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:31.770
We've definitely caused some damage on their side as well.

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:35.780
Just three goals~ We'll return them the favour.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:38.030
Is he for real?

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:45.540
Time's up. Alright, let's go.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:48.910
Wait, manager! What about actual instructions?

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:51.180
I don't have any.

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:54.170
We did this so many times during practice after all.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.700
What about motivating the players?

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.670
You can't send them out like this.

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:01.970
No matter what I say here, it won't have much effect.

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.950
They won't take it to heart.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:05.170
What?

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:07.180
It's fine.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:11.450
They'll naturally see the answer once they get onto the pitch.

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:14.380
Trust me.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:16.690
Alright, see ya!

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:31.020
Man, we're losing.

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:35.180
That's why I told you to come earlier!

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:37.040
I had no choice...

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:40.470
I had to go get this.

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:46.500
I guess this proves that they can't win without our support.

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:50.020
Shige, they lost even when we were there.

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:56.020
Hey, can we use the space in between?

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:58.530
We brought a banner, too.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:00.900
So could you shift yours a little bit?

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:04.910
You've got to be joking.

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:10.070
There are people who come to the stadium early to hang these up.

00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:12.660
You think you can just stroll in here this late and demand things?

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:19.240
We know that. We used to do that in the past, too.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:21.410
That's why we're asking you for a favor.

00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:24.170
You know, in the spirit of reciprocity?

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.300
No way.

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:30.560
We don't like people like you.

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:33.000
We don't want to be associated with you.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.560
What the hell?

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:39.190
The fans weren't like this during our time.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:41.190
Times have changed.

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:47.200
There is a difference between our support and yours.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:50.470
Why can't you just get that?

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:53.590
Difference between support?

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:55.520
What the hell's your problem?

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:58.590
So what, we can't even put up a single banner without your permission?

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:01.090
Who the hell do you think you are?

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:05.340
I knew you wouldn't understand.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:10.350
Hurry up, Hata! The players are coming out!

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:15.350
We'll never abandon the team, no matter what.

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:20.860
We'd rather die than become like you, Tanuma.

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:28.110
It starts here.

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:34.360
It's only two goals! Peg them back! Let this be a historical comeback win in ETU's folklore!

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:51.210
How did that guy... know my name?

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:58.480
Don't grab my collar in front of the younger players.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:01.720
It doesn't leave a good impression on me.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:04.330
Thanks, Kuro.

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:08.650
Thanks to you, I finally woke up. We can't let it end like this.

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:11.530
For our sakes as well.

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:18.220
Yeah. Let's do this, Sugie.

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:22.670
Both teams are sticking to the same lineup.

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:26.710
I guess Osaka will continue to dominate in this half as well.

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:28.050
Why?

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:28.800
Pardon?

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:31.300
Why do you think that?

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:37.060
Well, naturally. Since Osaka played really well...

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:39.540
I can never let my guard down...

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:42.020
The 1st half's history.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:44.900
A game lasts for 90 minutes.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:48.320
There's no way that nothing will change.

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:55.950
Furthermore, we haven't seen what Monsieur Tatsumi has in store for us.

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:03.210
Let's crush them again in this half!

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:05.670
Forwards, you all have to score!

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:09.610
Their lineup is basically the same.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:15.660
We have a two goal lead on you.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:18.930
What will you do?

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:24.440
Do you even have any idea how to turn things around, Tatsumi?

00:15:25.180 --> 00:15:31.050
No, you're someone who will try to win, especially in a situation like this.

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:33.890
My instinct as a manager tells me this...

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:38.450
You possess something which prompts me to give you everything I've got.

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:44.540
Otherwise, a rookie like you won't make me queer with such excitement.

00:15:45.940 --> 00:15:49.590
I never had the intention of having a great match with you.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:55.590
I just want to humiliate and annihilate men like you!

00:15:57.280 --> 00:15:58.470
I got it.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:01.740
Nice, Hiraga!

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:03.850
Keep depriving them of their chances!

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:05.770
Shimu!

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:11.270
The baldie and Hauer.

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:14.190
They're still sticking with this mismatch?

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:19.540
It's the same old story for this half as well!

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:20.700
Kuroda!

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:28.090
Don't make me run so much, Shimura. I finally got my hair right.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:34.220
They're aiming for Hauer right from the beginning.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:38.220
Well, I guess it makes sense, since he did score a goal.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:41.850
A centre-back allowing a goal...

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:44.730
That's like losing a one-on-one brawl.

00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:47.860
But you know...

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:50.230
Alright, I can control it!

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:55.610
Other than that goal, I don't feel that I'll lose to him in any way!

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.990
Damn baldie!

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:03.450
Ouch, Ref!

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:10.660
A foul by Hauer!

00:17:10.660 --> 00:17:12.460
Nice defending, Kuroda!

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:15.720
What? That was nothing!

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:19.180
Nice play, Kuroda. Hang in there!

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.970
He's getting more and more frustrated.

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:29.000
That means he knows.

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:32.980
He knows that he can't do anything without me getting in his way.

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:35.370
Nice, Kuroda!

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:37.240
Stay focused like this!

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:43.240
He blamed himself and Sugie for the goals we conceded in the 1st half,

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:48.000
but he's doing quite well, despite the difference in size.

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:52.500
Nah, he's not there yet.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:55.630
What? He is doing well!

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:58.550
Your expectations are too high, manager!

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:04.270
I'm pretty sure Kuro is starting to feel that things are going his way.

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:09.230
He changed his perspective from having not lost to having won.

00:18:10.140 --> 00:18:14.970
Our main objective today is whether or not we've enjoyed the game.

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:19.320
I'm certain that Kuro is starting to enjoy going up against Hauer.

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:24.310
When players enjoy themselves, they play incredibly well.

00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:26.620
That's why he's not there yet.

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:31.170
There's more to come from him.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:36.920
But we're two goals behind and we haven't had a proper attack yet.

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:38.040
Exactly.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:41.930
All our players need to start having the same feeling.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:44.980
Especially the guys up front.

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:47.180
Hey, Hauer!

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:50.910
Wasting a chance right from the start, what are you thinking?

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:54.420
I'm a forward. I can't finish a game without scoring!

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:57.190
Next time, try harder to pass the ball to me!

00:18:57.650 --> 00:18:59.700
He's noisy.

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:05.410
Forwards have to score, huh?

00:19:07.550 --> 00:19:10.510
What about me? I...

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:16.920
Stick with him, Akasaki! Don't let him get away so easily!

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:19.380
Shimu.

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:22.830
No good.

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:29.770
Kubo!

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:34.350
Kubota! Pass it to me!

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:36.110
Kubo! Send it to the left!

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:41.320
Alright, I'm going to enjoy this, just like the 1st half.

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:46.920
Sugie!

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.700
Great, Sugie!

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:53.220
What have I been looking at all the while?

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.720
What was I doing next to him?

00:19:56.850 --> 00:20:00.000
How could I even at look Kuro in the eye when, unlike me,

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:03.940
... he's been giving his all.

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:09.250
No, I can't stay this way.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:15.810
If I don't improve, how can ETU get stronger?!

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:19.690
Nice, Sugie! That's the spirit!

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:22.440
You're too slow! Get that ball!

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:23.700
Okay!

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:26.450
Gino!

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:28.450
Alright, to the front!

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:33.510
Natsuki!

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:35.900
Prince finally delivered a good pass!

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:37.130
Go!

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:38.880
Gino?

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:41.250
Alright!

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:43.760
He'll move into the centre, Lima!

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:48.710
Sera?

00:20:49.690 --> 00:20:50.890
Or Akasaki?

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:52.250
Or?

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:57.900
What are you doing, Natsuki?! Make up your mind!

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:03.360
Natsuki, you dwelled on the ball for too long!

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:06.360
Oh, shit.

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:15.210
G-Gino...

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:21.130
Nice, Tsubaki! Don't let them counter!

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:25.220
I guess their defense is getting used to us a bit.

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:29.140
However, their offense is totally disorganized.

00:21:29.670 --> 00:21:32.140
They're not linking up well at all.

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:34.890
10 minutes into the 2nd half.

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:37.930
We'll score the decisive third goal...

00:21:37.930 --> 00:21:40.710
and end the match comfortably.

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:46.900
Good! You're not allowing Hauer to turn around!

00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:49.910
You're so noisy!

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:51.410
Pass it here, Hauer!

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:55.040
Send me a high one. I can beat him in the air!

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:57.450
Shut up! Go make some space!

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:02.420
Hama, clear it!

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:03.420
Bastard!

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:06.800
That wasn't enough! Grab the loose ball!

00:22:15.940 --> 00:22:18.140
Good job, Sugie!

00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:21.060
We stopped Osaka's attacks!

00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:22.410
Alright.

00:22:22.410 --> 00:22:26.080
You were complicating matters in the 1st half,

00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:29.320
but I guess you've learnt, Sugie.

00:22:30.020 --> 00:22:32.820
I guess now the problem is him.

00:22:33.480 --> 00:22:35.190
Him?

00:22:36.740 --> 00:22:38.200
You mean Natsuki?

00:22:38.600 --> 00:22:41.860
Maybe it's because of what I told him before the game.

00:22:41.860 --> 00:22:46.080
Huh? What did you say to Natsuki?

00:22:46.080 --> 00:22:47.210
Hmm?

00:22:49.160 --> 00:22:50.720
I told him...

00:22:51.730 --> 00:22:55.960
that he lacks resolve as a forward.

00:24:15.130 --> 00:24:18.850
"Can you shoulder the hopes of your teammates and yet play for yourself at the same time?"

00:24:18.850 --> 00:24:22.080
That is the resolve of an egoistic forward.

00:24:22.080 --> 00:24:24.190
But that's also what makes a forward strong.

00:24:24.190 --> 00:24:25.220
Natsu.

00:24:25.220 --> 00:24:26.320
Akasaki!

00:24:26.320 --> 00:24:27.560
Let me shoot!
